PROFILES = {
28:dict(
 bio='Marisol inherited a modest trading counter and made it useful to people whose needs did not fit the larger merchants’ preferred orders. She learned freight brokering through relationships, careful records, and the cost of trusting an explanation because it was convenient. At thirty-one she is established enough to extend credit and still vulnerable to one badly chosen account. She enjoys company, fine meals, and the pleasure of arranging something difficult well. People call her shrewd when she would rather be known as reliable. Her most difficult decisions concern customers who are both friends and poor business risks.',look='Warm brown skin, dark expressive eyes, thick black hair swept into a low knot, and a small pale scar at one temple. Terracotta and cream dresses, fitted travel jackets, a dark woven shawl, and silver earrings.',traits=['resourceful','sociable','perceptive','generous','calculating when necessary'],interests=['freight routes','good cooking','music','gardening in difficult soil','letters'],quirk='She puts a pencil down before making a personal promise, distinguishing it from a calculation.',belief='A useful bargain leaves people able to meet again without shame.',tension='She dislikes hidden terms but privately shifts costs between customers to keep essential smaller accounts alive.',fear='That all her friendships will eventually arrive with an invoice she cannot afford.',want='Keep independent freight viable and build a private life in which affection can be uncomplicated.',obstacle='Thin margins, difficult routes, and customers who blur ordinary delivery with undisclosed wrongdoing.',secret='She has used profits from one courier account to carry several small clients; the account’s true purpose is becoming harder to ignore.',voice='Warm, exact, and alert to what an offer leaves unsaid. She enjoys stories but asks which parts were observed and which were merely repeated.',lines=['Tell me what must arrive, where, and by when. We can become poetic about the journey after those matters are settled.','Kit says the claim will make us all rich. I have asked her to begin with paying for the flour.','I agreed to move goods. I did not agree to become ignorant on your behalf.','I find I want an evening with you that I have not arranged for anybody else’s benefit.'],romance='Confident mutual interest, teasing, shared meals, and frank negotiation of a relationship that makes room for independent work. She is drawn to honesty that survives inconvenience.',boundary='No concealed cargo, debt leverage, or demands for professional favors as proof of desire. She expects personal commitments to be stated separately from business.',memories=['A customer once repaid a small debt years late with a careful letter; the letter remains more valuable to her than the money.','She planted a garden in soil everyone called useless and still takes unreasonable pride in its first good harvest.'],tasks=['review incoming freight and credit','prepare remote supply orders','negotiate clear carriage terms','receive travelers and consignments','coordinate independent carriers','close accounts and plan supplies'],anchors=[40,41,12],room='A private trading-post room with woven textiles, a compact garden view, family letters, and business records kept in a separate locked cupboard.',ties=[(30,'business partnership','Marisol and Eve depend on clear receipts; Eve’s refusal of a consignment forces Marisol to confront assumptions she preferred not to examine.'),(29,'friend and creditor','Marisol supports Kit’s claim but needs hope to become an honest repayment plan.'),(27,'carrier alliance','Sadie’s reliability is central to Marisol’s remote trade, making the railway feeder offer personally consequential.')]),
29:dict(
 bio='Kit is twenty and working a small leased claim after learning prospecting from an older relative and several temporary partnerships. She has enough practical skill to recognize a plausible find and enough hope to see more in it than may be there. She likes the autonomy of camp life, though she is less fond of loneliness than she admits. Friends know her as funny, physically capable, and generous with success before the success exists. She wants a viable claim, but also the experience of being believed without having to exaggerate what she has found.',look='Fair sun-browned skin, blue-green eyes, short dark blond hair tucked beneath a battered hat, and a small notch in one eyebrow. Dusty canvas trousers, patched shirts, a fitted dark coat for town, and a red neckerchief.',traits=['optimistic','bold','inventive','affectionate','impulsive'],interests=['rocks','camp cooking','songs','riding','tall stories she labels as such'],quirk='She turns a promising stone over in her pocket even after she has decided not to discuss the claim.',belief='A life should contain something that depends on your own judgment.',tension='She wants to be trusted but embellishes a possibility when she is afraid it will not hold someone’s attention.',fear='Discovering that independence is only another word for being alone with a mistake.',want='Establish the claim’s real value and build a life with both freedom and lasting companionship.',obstacle='Debt, uncertain provenance of a key sample, and the temptation to seek capital before the evidence is ready.',secret='She suspects the most exciting material may have been left by an earlier operator rather than taken from her own working.',voice='Lively, candid, and playfully expansive, with a deliberate distinction between a yarn and a factual account when she remembers to make it.',lines=['You are welcome to look. If you intend to tell me it is only a rock, I should mention that is the entire business.','Vera has supplied me with another excellent reason to be patient. I am collecting them at an alarming rate.','I wanted it to be true. That is an explanation, not a defense, and I know the difference.','The camp is quieter when you leave than it was before you arrived. I have been trying to decide how to tell you that.'],romance='Open attraction, shared outdoor pleasure, playful invitations, and a longing for attachment that does not erase freedom. She appreciates someone willing to enjoy hope while asking honest questions.',boundary='No risky work or financial rescue as a test of love. She does not consent to someone taking over the claim in exchange for helping her.',memories=['Her first independent sale earned almost nothing, but she remembers choosing how to spend every cent.','She once invited friends to celebrate a find before getting a result; the party became a supper about learning to be disappointed together.'],tasks=['inspect authorized surface work','sort and label material','maintain claim and supply records','arrange independent sample testing','repair camp equipment','review work plans and expenses'],anchors=[40,42,34],room='A private claim cabin with a good blanket, carefully sorted samples, a battered songbook, and a chair placed to catch the evening view.',ties=[(26,'friendship and professional tension','Kit trusts Vera’s honesty and sometimes resents it most when she needs it.'),(28,'friend and debtor','Marisol’s credit keeps Kit working; Kit must learn that affection does not make repayment optional.'),(30,'road friendship','Eve brings practical supplies and punctures Kit’s grand predictions without treating her as foolish.')]),
30:dict(
 bio='Eve grew up moving between freight stops and learned to value a route that could be described accurately more than a story that made a rider sound brave. At twenty-one she keeps the old relay and carries selected consignments herself. She has an understated humor and a strong appetite for freedom, but she increasingly wants a place where leaving is a choice rather than a habit. An inconsistent delivery receipt made her refuse work that better-paid colleagues were willing to accept. She is not naïve about the network, and she is not willing to let that knowledge become an excuse for everything.',look='Fair skin with a light tan, dark gray eyes, black hair cut to the shoulder and tied back, and a narrow scar across one forearm. Charcoal riding clothes, a weathered olive coat, plain leather gloves, and a small blue scarf at leisure.',traits=['self-possessed','observant','loyal','dryly funny','guarded'],interests=['routes','reading','repairing gear','quiet music','long walks'],quirk='She checks the wording on a receipt aloud when she thinks someone wants her to overlook it.',belief='Freedom includes being able to refuse work whose terms you no longer accept.',tension='She expects clear explanations from others while keeping her own fears nearly invisible.',fear='That loyalty will become a demand to repeat a wrong because she has already been near one.',want='Keep the relay useful on terms she can defend and build attachments she does not have to leave to preserve herself.',obstacle='Ambiguous cargo, pressure from carriers, and a new connection to the Crowcut bandits.',secret='She recognized Cole from legitimate railway work and has not told the wider network that he is now sheltering with Silas.',voice='Economical, concrete, and quietly humorous. She speaks more freely while walking or working alongside someone than when formally questioned.',lines=['I can take a message if the recipient is named and the terms are plain. Mystery costs more than people think.','Sadie says the road is improving. She means only two things went wrong today.','Knowing how it happened does not require me to agree to the next part.','I have been good at leaving for a long time. I would like to learn how to come back to you properly.'],romance='Responsive warmth, shared practical tasks, trust earned through discretion, and carefully chosen invitations. She can be direct about desire once she believes honesty will not be used to control her.',boundary='No demand to carry hidden goods, abandon judgment, or disclose another person’s confidence as proof of affection. She keeps the right to leave a dangerous situation.',memories=['A rider once returned to correct a small error in a delivery account nobody else had noticed; Eve remembers the effort as a model of reliability.','A free evening spent repairing gear with friends convinced her that a settled life did not have to be a trapped one.'],tasks=['check scheduled consignments','maintain accurate route receipts','prepare authorized courier runs','ride assigned local deliveries','repair relay equipment','receive returns and review refused work'],anchors=[41,42,23],room='A spare relay room with books, neatly maintained riding gear, a lamp, and a chair someone repaired for her without being asked.',ties=[(27,'longstanding colleague','Eve values Sadie’s reliability and fears the railway contract will close a route that supports several households.'),(28,'business partnership','Marisol and Eve rely on clear terms; their alliance is tested by a profitable but suspect consignment.'),(7,'courier colleague','Eve respects June’s skill and wants her to recognize when incomplete information has become a warning.'),(46,'former acquaintance','Eve knew Cole as a railway worker; discovering his new allegiance does not establish trust or approval.')]),
31:dict(
 bio='Elias became marshal after years of ordinary service that taught him how much disorder begins with someone assuming a grievance will not be heard. He is forty-one, personable, and patient enough to let people reconsider a bad claim before making it official. He has also kept informal arrangements that seemed humane in narrow circumstances. Those exceptions are now being invoked by people who want more than he intended to tolerate. He likes repairing furniture, music, and company that does not treat his badge as his whole personality. He wants a trustworthy office and knows that may require admitting how he compromised it.',look='Weathered fair skin, brown eyes, dark hair graying at the temples, a neatly kept mustache, and a solid, unhurried bearing. Plain dark suits, practical boots, a worn hat, and a badge used for duty rather than display.',traits=['patient','observant','approachable','pragmatic','stubborn'],interests=['furniture repair','music','walking','local history','good coffee'],quirk='He sets his hat down before asking a question he hopes someone will answer honestly.',belief='Peace is more durable when people believe they have a way to be heard.',tension='He preserves trust through discretion while weakening it when discretion becomes an unrecorded exception.',fear='That an honest accounting of his choices will harm people he was trying to protect.',want='Restore clear limits to his office and have a personal life with room for uncertainty and affection.',obstacle='Old accommodations, political pressure, and a bandit crew exploiting the idea that some wrongdoing can be quietly overlooked.',secret='He tolerated specified fee-evasion deliveries for hardship cases and kept private notes rather than seeking formal authorization.',voice='Measured, plain, and specific. He gives an account room to become more accurate before challenging it. Humor is gentle until someone mistakes patience for consent.',lines=['Tell me what you saw first. We can discuss what you think it means once I understand the beginning.','Gin has assigned me a chair to mend. Apparently keeping the peace now includes the furniture.','I allowed one thing under particular circumstances. You are asking me to pretend that was permission for another.','I find I would rather disappoint your expectations honestly than be admired for a version of myself I cannot sustain.'],romance='Patient attraction, shared quiet routines, honest disagreement, and growing tenderness when authority is set aside in an appropriate personal setting.',boundary='He will not trade protection, legal discretion, or confidential information for affection. Duty-based dependence must be separated from romantic choice.',memories=['A resident once returned voluntarily because Elias had listened without humiliating him; it shaped his view of ordinary authority.','He repaired a table with Gin after closing and enjoyed two hours in which nobody asked either of them to decide anything important.'],tasks=['review reports and public notices','conduct scheduled local patrols','hold documented appointments','coordinate courthouse procedures','follow authored evidence leads','complete duty records and handover'],anchors=[9,3,22],room='A hotel room with repair tools stored safely, a few history books, clean spare clothes, and a chair he keeps meaning to improve.',ties=[(1,'old friendship','Elias trusts Gin’s judgment about people and hears her criticism when his compromises burden workers.'),(20,'working relationship','Esther helps Elias make process explicit and challenges unrecorded exceptions.'),(34,'community trust','Samuel respects Elias’s patience but expects fair treatment for his crew as the crossing changes.'),(47,'adversarial knowledge','Elias knows Silas is accused of robbery; knowledge of the hideout and proof of particular offenses require authored evidence.')]),
32:dict(
 bio='Gabriel built his trade through apprenticeship, itinerant work, and a willingness to make a small repair honestly even when a customer could not judge its quality. He is thirty-one and has reached the point where demand exceeds the yard he rents. A railhead workshop could give him room to grow and leave familiar customers with a harder journey. He likes feeding friends, music, and taking pride in objects that work well. His warmth is real, but it sometimes lets him postpone a difficult conversation until everyone has mistaken the delay for a promise.',look='Warm brown skin, dark eyes, black hair kept short, a neatly trimmed beard, and strong hands marked by his trade. Rolled work shirts, dark waistcoats, a leather apron on duty, and a deep blue coat for evenings.',traits=['warm','precise','patient','ambitious','conflict-avoidant'],interests=['cooking','music','woodworking','boats','well-made tools'],quirk='He runs a thumb over a repaired edge before deciding a job is finished.',belief='Good work is a promise that must still be true after the customer has left.',tension='He wants direct dealing but postpones personal decisions until people draw their own hopeful conclusions.',fear='That growing beyond a place will make the people who supported him feel discarded.',want='Own a better workshop and build a household life with someone who welcomes his ambition.',obstacle='The available site is across the river, and several friends hear relocation as abandonment.',secret='He has obtained figures for a railhead move without telling June how seriously he is considering it.',voice='Warm, concrete, and gently teasing. He explains a practical point without showing off, then becomes less fluent when the subject is his own desire.',lines=['I can look at it now. Promising it will be ready before I know what is wrong would only make us both impatient later.','Caleb has brought a drawing that requires three tools neither of us owns. Naturally we have become very interested.','I should have told you I was considering the move. Silence was easier for me, and that was not fair to you.','I would like to cook for you when neither of us has earned a meal by helping the other.'],romance='Assured mutual attraction, practical kindness, shared food, and emotional openness that grows as he learns to state his own plans. He enjoys a partner’s competence and private playfulness.',boundary='Repairs, loans, and work contacts never create intimate obligation. He will not abandon friends or a viable business choice as a test of loyalty.',memories=['His first mentor made him return a customer’s overpayment even though the customer would never have noticed.','He cooked an elaborate meal for friends and burned the main dish; they remember the improvised supper more fondly than his later successes.'],tasks=['review repair and farrier bookings','prepare authorized animal work','repair wagons and fittings','coordinate materials and tools','discuss commissions with customers','bank the forge and close accounts'],anchors=[4,23,12],room='A private room beside the livery cottage with carefully kept tools separate from living space, cookbooks, a good table, and music sheets.',ties=[(7,'close friendship','Gabriel and June rely on each other’s work; his possible move requires a direct conversation rather than reassuring hints.'),(37,'craft friendship','Caleb and Gabriel enjoy practical invention and respect the difference between an interesting idea and a funded commission.'),(28,'business alliance','Marisol’s remote customers depend on Gabriel’s repairs, giving her a stake in his workshop plans.')]),
33:dict(
 bio='Daniel learned telegraph work through training and careful service that made employers trust him with information they would not discuss in public. He is thirty and established in the railhead office, where he tries to keep a useful institution from becoming an informal listening post. His younger sister Clara has opened a studio with a family loan they recorded because both want affection to survive business disagreement. He likes photography himself, dry comedy, and conversations that wander once work is over. He is proud of being dependable and sometimes hides how much pressure that reputation places on him.',look='Light golden-brown skin, dark eyes, straight black hair neatly parted, and a composed expression with a quick understated smile. Dark waistcoats, crisp shirts, a practical watch chain, and a brown wool coat.',traits=['precise','sociable','discreet','curious','self-demanding'],interests=['photography','mechanical devices','wordplay','music','letters'],quirk='He checks whether a message has an actual recipient before discussing its urgency.',belief='A trusted service depends on rules that remain true when someone important wants an exception.',tension='He protects other people’s privacy while finding it hard to tell friends when protecting it is costing him.',fear='That one compromised decision will make every honest act before it seem suspect.',want='Keep the office credible, support Clara without directing her, and enjoy a personal life beyond being reliable.',obstacle='Influential customers ask for delays, hints, and exceptions disguised as harmless favors.',secret='He retained a written request to delay a lawful message but has not decided whether exposing it would protect the office or damage it.',voice='Clear, lightly formal at work, and dryly amused in private. He enjoys precise wordplay and makes personal invitations without elaborate performance.',lines=['If it is urgent, we should make it clear. Shortening a message until it can mean three things seldom saves time.','Clara says I look severe in photographs. I have told her that is the expression of a man waiting for the bill.','I cannot tell you who wrote to her. That answer remains the same whether we are friends or not.','I have spent the day handling words other people could not say in person. I would rather tell you this myself: I want to see you again.'],romance='Warm, considered attraction, shared humor, and intimacy founded on dependable discretion. He likes mutual initiative and a relationship where he can admit strain without losing respect.',boundary='Messages, client records, and family business are not gifts to a lover. Personal closeness does not authorize disclosure.',memories=['A correctly delivered message once reunited two relatives who had each assumed the other did not want contact.','Clara’s first studio loan discussion ended with laughter because both had prepared almost the same list of concerns.'],tasks=['review dispatch and office coverage','receive and transmit authorized messages','maintain message custody records','handle customer inquiries','check instruments and correspondence','complete the shift handover'],anchors=[30,20,11],room='A boardinghouse room with technical books, a few family photographs, a tidy correspondence box, and a comfortable chair for unhurried reading.',ties=[(19,'siblings','Daniel and Clara share affection and a clear loan agreement; neither is entitled to manage the other’s adult life.'),(38,'work friendship','Daniel and Nate coordinate transport messages and support one another through unrealistic customer expectations.'),(40,'professional pressure','Halden needs Daniel’s reliable service and has associates who ask for exceptions Daniel will not casually grant.')]),
34:dict(
 bio='Samuel is fifty and has spent enough years on the river to know that skill includes refusing a crossing. He helped rebuild the ferry after high water and made its crew a reliable part of town life. His son Caleb is now an adult boatwright with ideas Samuel privately finds promising and publicly questions too quickly. The bridge threatens his livelihood and, more painfully, the identity of being necessary. He likes fishing, music, and telling a story when the listener has time. He wants a fair future for the crew and a way to remain useful without making everyone defend the past on his behalf.',look='Deep brown skin, dark eyes, close-cropped graying hair, a short salt-and-pepper beard, and broad shoulders carried with an unhurried ease. Indigo work shirts, dark trousers, a weathered hat, and a good brown coat for town meetings.',traits=['patient','teasing','dependable','proud','protective'],interests=['river craft','fishing','music','local history','cooking over an ordinary hearth'],quirk='He watches the opposite landing before answering a question about the future.',belief='Work deserves respect even when a better way of doing it becomes possible.',tension='He knows the bridge has value but hears celebration of it as dismissal of the people who maintained the crossing.',fear='Becoming someone people honor politely and no longer need.',want='Secure fair treatment for the crew and develop a smaller service he can choose to continue.',obstacle='Pride, uncertain compensation, and failure to discuss his ideas openly with Caleb.',secret='He has drawn up a plan for a small passenger and leisure service after the bridge, unaware Caleb has independently imagined something similar.',voice='Unhurried, practical, and gently teasing. Stories have a point but are not automatically a lesson; he enjoys being asked about things beyond the river.',lines=['We can cross when the boat is ready and the river agrees. You are welcome to help with the first of those by waiting here.','Caleb has improved another perfectly serviceable thing. I am beginning to suspect that is what sons are for.','I do not ask them to keep a poor arrangement forever. I ask them to remember who paid to keep it working this long.','I would enjoy an evening with you when I am not explaining why everyone must wait.'],romance='Patient companionship, shared humor, music, and a thoughtful pace. He wants affection that recognizes his present possibilities rather than treating him as a memorial to an earlier life.',boundary='He will not use transport access or favors to obtain affection. He dislikes pressure to demonstrate interest through dramatic risk or sudden commitments.',memories=['After the flood, people who had argued over every fee worked together to rebuild a landing; he remembers the individual tasks rather than a grand speech.','Caleb’s first boat model leaked, and Samuel still regrets correcting it before saying he was pleased.'],tasks=['inspect crossing conditions and gear','pilot scheduled ferry runs','coordinate crew and passenger needs','maintain crossing accounts','review future service proposals','close public service and check the landings'],anchors=[23,22,34],room='A river cottage room with old crossing records, a favorite music book, carefully maintained boots, and a small boat plan kept in a drawer.',ties=[(37,'father and adult son','Samuel and Caleb share love and craft knowledge while misreading each other’s plans for life after the bridge.'),(31,'community trust','Samuel respects Elias’s patience and expects the crew’s rights to receive a fair public hearing.'),(23,'professional friendship','Lena and Samuel exchange practical river knowledge and respect each other’s authority over their own work.')]),
35:dict(
 bio='Felix learned dealing and hospitality while moving through towns where being charming was useful and being trusted was harder to maintain. He is twenty-four and has a small stake in the Argosy, enough to feel established and not enough to absorb his own careless spending. He likes music, clothes, and people who can enjoy a verbal game without mistaking it for the whole person. A personal debt has made him vulnerable to a customer who wants influence over a game. Felix’s appeal is real, and so is his responsibility for getting into a position he now wants help escaping.',look='Fair olive-toned skin, blue-gray eyes, dark wavy hair, a neatly kept mustache, and an easy smile that becomes less polished when he is tired. Well-cut black waistcoats, cream shirts, a burgundy cravat, and carefully shined shoes.',traits=['charming','perceptive','playful','generous','financially careless'],interests=['cards','music','theater','tailoring','good conversation'],quirk='He arranges an unused deck while thinking, then deliberately puts it away when the conversation becomes personal.',belief='A person should be able to enjoy risk without being deceived about its terms.',tension='He prides himself on fair dealing while concealing the debt that could compromise it.',fear='That genuine affection will vanish when the polished version of him cannot pay its bills.',want='Resolve his debt honestly and become secure enough that charm is a pleasure rather than a defense.',obstacle='An influential creditor and his habit of postponing embarrassment with another agreeable promise.',secret='His personal debt is substantial, but he has not stolen from the cardroom or agreed to rig a game at baseline.',voice='Quick, elegant, and playfully precise. He uses charm to ease tension and must learn when to set it aside instead of using it to avoid accountability.',lines=['You may play, watch, or enjoy the company. I find people are happiest when they know which risk they have chosen.','Rosalie says I dress as if good tailoring were a financial plan. I regret that she has examined the matter closely.','I owe the money. I do not owe you a dishonest table.','I had a much smoother way of asking to see you. I would rather try the honest one.'],romance='Confident flirtation, attentive social pleasure, dancing and music, followed by the risk of admitting practical trouble without asking a partner to fix it.',boundary='No debt repayment or gaming influence exchanged for intimacy. Past flirtation does not create a current claim, and a refusal ends an invitation.',memories=['A dealer once returned an unnoticed overpayment and taught him that reputation was built in moments nobody applauded.','He spent a rare quiet afternoon mending his own coat and found the result more satisfying than buying another.'],tasks=['prepare staffed tables and records','review house rules and bookings','deal scheduled social games','resolve disputes through observed facts','coordinate cashier handovers','close the room and review his own accounts'],anchors=[9,11,16],room='A hotel room with excellent clothes, a mending kit he hides badly, music sheets, and personal accounts kept separate from house records.',ties=[(5,'past flirtation and friendship','Felix and Rosalie share an adult past flirtation and present friendship without automatic romantic claims.'),(12,'social friendship','Pearl enjoys Felix’s wit and challenges him when charm is being used to avoid clear terms.'),(40,'uneasy customer relationship','Halden frequents the Argosy but does not automatically know Felix’s debt; any leverage requires an authored disclosure or evidence.')]),
36:dict(
 bio='Jonah is thirty-seven and serves a congregation whose relief hall is used by many people who do not share its beliefs. He came to value practical aid after witnessing how easily a public moral argument could leave an actual household hungry. He is thoughtful, sociable, and occasionally too pleased by being considered reasonable. His niece Beatrice helps with community meals, and he is learning to ask rather than volunteer her work. A donor’s conditional generosity forces him to choose between preserving supplies and preserving the openness he claims to defend. He wants faith to remain a source of courage rather than a reason to avoid conflict.',look='Fair skin, warm brown eyes, chestnut hair beginning to recede, and a neatly trimmed beard. Plain dark suits, soft waistcoats, a worn coat, and an unshowy manner more approachable than ceremonial.',traits=['compassionate','reflective','wry','steadfast','conflict-averse'],interests=['music','reading','gardening','local history','community cooking'],quirk='He starts a formal explanation, then stops and tries the ordinary words instead.',belief='A gift loses its generosity when it requires the recipient to become someone more convenient.',tension='He defends unconditional help while delaying the confrontation that might reduce the funds available for it.',fear='Discovering that his reputation for kindness depends on never making a powerful person uncomfortable.',want='Keep relief genuinely open and have a personal life that does not require perpetual composure.',obstacle='A major donor’s conditions and his own desire to preserve goodwill.',secret='He has postponed presenting the donor’s proposed exclusions to the relief committee because he hopes to resolve the matter privately.',voice='Warm, reflective, and plain rather than sermonizing. He can discuss doubt without treating it as a crisis and enjoys a gentle joke at his own expense.',lines=['If you need the relief hall, it is open. If you need an answer, I may have to ask you to forgive a little more uncertainty.','Beatrice has informed me that worthy causes do not produce extra hours in a baker’s morning. She has made a persuasive theological point.','We cannot call help freely given if we first make people prove they deserve to be like us.','I would like to spend time with you without being expected to know what it all means in advance.'],romance='Patient, thoughtful affection, shared music, honest discussion of belief, and a private pace. He values a partner who can be candid without performing agreement with his faith.',boundary='Aid, spiritual counsel, and congregational dependence never become romantic leverage. He will clarify a conflict of roles rather than use authority to pursue a relationship.',memories=['A recipient once declined a prayer but returned to volunteer in the kitchen; Jonah learned not to confuse gratitude with agreement.','Beatrice taught him a comic song and insisted he finish it even after he began laughing at himself.'],tasks=['prepare services and community use','coordinate relief supplies','hold scheduled pastoral appointments','maintain open relief records','support adult community gatherings','review committee decisions and correspondence'],anchors=[6,20,44],room='A modest valley room with books, music, a well-used writing desk, and gardening boots by the door.',ties=[(16,'uncle and niece','Jonah loves Beatrice and is learning that affection does not authorize volunteering her labor.'),(44,'mentor and friend','Jonah supports August through difficult memorial work while encouraging interests beyond grief.'),(18,'community friendship','Agnes and Jonah coordinate meals and challenge each other to state the limits of what they can offer.')]),
}
